block requests a Mid Red retry for that one row.

Second known conflict (row 7 of the same gate): under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce every
element must report a computed transition-duration of 0 s, but the read-along package
words and sentences carry unconditional Tailwind duration-150/duration-200 (the committed
build chunk shows .duration-150{transition-duration:.15s}; motion-reduce:transition-none
clears the property only). Zeroing them needs a transition-duration declaration under
reduce, and look-reduced-motion.test.ts rejects every transition-* declaration of look.css
outside a pure (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) block (the media check is an exact
array-element match, so a `not (...)` spelling does not pass it). The in-scope files cannot
carry the fix: globals.css is song-stage rules only (section 2.2.2) and the package path is
allowed for a data attribute only (closeout item 3). The final block routes this to the
orchestrator with the options.



